          "Sampling Frame: Municipality population registers \n\nSampling Design: A stratified two-stage probability design. Municipalities were selected as PSUs with probability proportional to population size (aged 15+), with replacement. This means that municipalities could be sampled multiple times. The 200 selections correspond to 179 distinct municipalities. Strata were defined by the cross-classification of district of residence (NUTS3) and size of municipality. At the second stage, m*120 individuals aged 15+ were selected by systematic random sampling from each municipality, where m is the number of times the municipality was selected at the first stage)."
