          "Sampling Frame: Municipality population registers\n\nSampling Design: A two-domain stratified two-stage probability design. The first domain consisted of the 15 largest municipalities in Germany. In this domain, a systematic (unclustered) random sample of individuals was selected, proportionately stratified by municipality. In the second domain, consisting of the remainder of the country, 166 municipalities were selected as PSUs with probability proportional to population size (aged 15+) and an equal number of individuals was subsequently selected at random from each selected municipality. "
